{
  "reason": "Use Tier 2: decouple SASRec’s context embeddings from its candidate-scoring embeddings. The historical ensemble and 16-negative objective reached 0.6200, while subsequent fusion changes regressed and auxiliary VAE supervision recovered only to 0.5900; this motivates testing a new representation component rather than another fusion adjustment. Shared SASRec embeddings receive both context-encoding and candidate-classification gradients, creating a possible capacity bottleneck that this controlled experiment can test.",
  "module": [
    "model_design",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Make one architectural change: add an independent SASRec output_emb table for positive, negative, and inference candidate scoring, retaining item_emb exclusively for sequence inputs. Initialize output_emb with nn.Embedding.from_pretrained(self.item_emb.weight.detach().clone(), freeze=False, padding_idx=0) after existing initialization, preserving initial embedding values without consuming additional random draws. Update SASRec.forward and SASRec.predict to retrieve candidate vectors from output_emb while leaving log2feats, function signatures, constructor arguments, hidden dimensions, and the positive-plus-16-negative cross-entropy unchanged. Preserve MultVAE reconstruction, auxiliary continuation supervision, history processing, and the current rank_fusion rule so the experiment isolates embedding separation.",
    "training_evaluation": "Keep train_sasrec and its optimizer settings unchanged; model.parameters() must include output_emb, and checkpoints must save and strictly reload the additional table through the updated SASRec class. Preserve load_ensemble and write_predict_script signatures, updating generated predictor documentation so working/predict.py reconstructs the new architecture and shares the same candidate-scoring implementation as validation. Add isolated checks that the two tables initially match but have independent storage, receive finite gradients, and produce matching predictions after checkpoint reload; retain generated-predictor agreement checks. Preserve all four dataset routes, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], supplied splits, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, single-GPU deadlines, and trial-local artifacts. Evaluate unchanged HR@10 with evaluation seed 42, 200 users per category, and 99 unique negatives, report measured macro performance against 0.5900 and historical 0.6200, and print the actual Final Validation Score without accessing hidden tests or changing the host evaluator."
  }
